{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017EbahFjScrvL6vxxaXrL5B","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Brief: tap-to-complete on the \"Your Day\" widget\n2\t\n3\ttype: feature\n4\tid: motivation\n5\tbranch: feature/motivation_tap-to-complete-on-the-your-day-widget\n6\tdate: 2026-10-29\n7\tauthor: Leander Muskalla\n8\t\n9\t## What\n10\t\n11\tTodo rows on the Your Day widget get a checkbox. Tapping it completes the\n12\ttodo on the server and updates the widget. This is built as generic action\n13\tplumbing that every later interactive widget reuses.\n14\t\n15\tThis is job 6 of 6 in `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets-decisions.md`\n16\t(D3, D8, D11). Read that document first. It depends on\n17\t[[android-widget-foundation-your-day]] and on the API's\n18\t`POST /widgets/actions/todo.complete/{todo}`.\n19\t\n20\t## Why\n21\t\n22\tCompleting a todo is the most common thing users do on Your Day. Building it\n23\tnow also proves the interaction path (intents, background calls, error and\n24\trevert states) before other widgets depend on it.\n25\t\n26\t## Contract with the API\n27\t\n28\tThe API lives in another repo and is not visible from here. This section is\n29\tthe complete contract this job relies on; the widget data format, headers and\n30\tgeneral status codes are in [[android-widget-foundation-your-day]].\n31\t\n32\tRows that can be acted on carry, for example:\n33\t`\"action\": { \"type\": \"check\", \"key\": \"todo.complete\", \"checked\": false }`.\n34\t\n35\tRequest: `POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/{key}/{id}`, for example\n36\t`POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/todo.complete/<todo uuid>`, with the same\n37\theaders as the widget fetch (`Authorization: Bearer <widget token>`,\n38\t`Accept: application/json`, `X-Client-Version`) and no body.\n39\t\n40\t| Status | Meaning | Native does |\n41\t|---|---|---|\n42\t| 200 | Done (envelope with `data: null`). Also returned when the todo was already completed: the action is idempotent | Re-fetch all placed widgets |\n43\t| 401 | Widget token invalid or expired | Delete the local token, show the signed-out state |\n44\t| 403 | The todo belongs to someone else (should not happen from widget data) | Treat like 404 |\n45\t| 404 | The todo no longer exists, or the server has no such action | Re-fetch |\n46\t| 426 | App below the server's minimum version | Revert the row, show \"Please update the app\" |\n47\t| 429 / 5xx / no response | Rate-limited, server or network problem | Revert the row, show a short error state |\n48\t\n49\tCompleting a recurring todo creates its next occurrence on the server; the\n50\tre-fetch shows it if it is due. There is no \"uncomplete\" action.\n51\t\n52\t## Steps\n53\t\n54\t1. **Generic action handling:** rows with\n55\t   `action: { type, key, checked? }`. Native knows UI **types** only; for now\n56\t   `check`. Rows with an unknown type render without the control. The `key`\n57\t   is posted as-is to `POST /widgets/actions/{key}/{id}` after validating its\n58\t   format (`[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]*`) and the id; native has no per-key code.\n59\t2. **Checkbox:** on API 31+ a real checkbox (`setCompoundButtonChecked` +\n60\t   `RemoteViews.RemoteResponse`); on 24–30 a tappable checkbox icon. Same\n61\t   behaviour on both.\n62\t3. **Flow:** tap → explicit, non-exported receiver (fill-in extras are\n63\t   untrusted: validate them) → the row shows as done at once → an expedited\n64\t   WorkManager job calls the action with the widget token (read from the\n65\t   token store, not from input data) → on success re-fetch all placed widgets.\n66\t4. **Errors (D11):**\n67\t   - 404: the todo is gone, re-fetch;\n68\t   - 401: signed-out state, delete the local token;\n69\t   - offline, 429, 5xx: revert the row and show a short error state on the\n70\t     widget; nothing is queued for later;\n71\t   - repeated taps while a call is running are ignored for that row.\n72\t   The server action is idempotent, so a retry after a lost response is safe.\n73\t5. **Strings** (`values`, `values-de/fr/es/it`): the error text and the\n74\t   checkbox's content description.\n75\t6. **Manual checks:** complete a todo (API 24 and 34+); complete a recurring\n76\t   todo (the next occurrence appears after the re-fetch if it is due);\n77\t   airplane mode (revert + error); complete a todo deleted in the app\n78\t   meanwhile (row disappears); double tap; complete in the widget, then open\n79\t   the app (the todo shows as completed).\n80\t\n81\t## Out of scope\n82\t\n83\t- Uncompleting from the widget (the server has no such action).\n84\t- A retry queue for offline taps.\n85\t- Actions on other rows or other widgets.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1bd9fed-904f-4ef7-b990-1d5b7016b4d3","uuid":"cd8247fc-6698-4cd1-9263-4482c7de8441","timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:56:53.767Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/motivation_tap-to-complete-on-the-your-day-widget/brief.md","content":"# Brief: tap-to-complete on the \"Your Day\" widget\n\ntype: feature\nid: motivation\nbranch: feature/motivation_tap-to-complete-on-the-your-day-widget\ndate: 2026-10-29\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nTodo rows on the Your Day widget get a checkbox. Tapping it completes the\ntodo on the server and updates the widget. This is built as generic action\nplumbing that every later interactive widget reuses.\n\nThis is job 6 of 6 in `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets-decisions.md`\n(D3, D8, D11). Read that document first. It depends on\n[[android-widget-foundation-your-day]] and on the API's\n`POST /widgets/actions/todo.complete/{todo}`.\n\n## Why\n\nCompleting a todo is the most common thing users do on Your Day. Building it\nnow also proves the interaction path (intents, background calls, error and\nrevert states) before other widgets depend on it.\n\n## Contract with the API\n\nThe API lives in another repo and is not visible from here. This section is\nthe complete contract this job relies on; the widget data format, headers and\ngeneral status codes are in [[android-widget-foundation-your-day]].\n\nRows that can be acted on carry, for example:\n`\"action\": { \"type\": \"check\", \"key\": \"todo.complete\", \"checked\": false }`.\n\nRequest: `POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/{key}/{id}`, for example\n`POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/todo.complete/<todo uuid>`, with the same\nheaders as the widget fetch (`Authorization: Bearer <widget token>`,\n`Accept: application/json`, `X-Client-Version`) and no body.\n\n| Status | Meaning | Native does |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 | Done (envelope with `data: null`). Also returned when the todo was already completed: the action is idempotent | Re-fetch all placed widgets |\n| 401 | Widget token invalid or expired | Delete the local token, show the signed-out state |\n| 403 | The todo belongs to someone else (should not happen from widget data) | Treat like 404 |\n| 404 | The todo no longer exists, or the server has no such action | Re-fetch |\n| 426 | App below the server's minimum version | Revert the row, show \"Please update the app\" |\n| 429 / 5xx / no response | Rate-limited, server or network problem | Revert the row, show a short error state |\n\nCompleting a recurring todo creates its next occurrence on the server; the\nre-fetch shows it if it is due. There is no \"uncomplete\" action.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Generic action handling:** rows with\n   `action: { type, key, checked? }`. Native knows UI **types** only; for now\n   `check`. Rows with an unknown type render without the control. The `key`\n   is posted as-is to `POST /widgets/actions/{key}/{id}` after validating its\n   format (`[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]*`) and the id; native has no per-key code.\n2. **Checkbox:** on API 31+ a real checkbox (`setCompoundButtonChecked` +\n   `RemoteViews.RemoteResponse`); on 24–30 a tappable checkbox icon. Same\n   behaviour on both.\n3. **Flow:** tap → explicit, non-exported receiver (fill-in extras are\n   untrusted: validate them) → the row shows as done at once → an expedited\n   WorkManager job calls the action with the widget token (read from the\n   token store, not from input data) → on success re-fetch all placed widgets.\n4. **Errors (D11):**\n   - 404: the todo is gone, re-fetch;\n   - 401: signed-out state, delete the local token;\n   - offline, 429, 5xx: revert the row and show a short error state on the\n     widget; nothing is queued for later;\n   - repeated taps while a call is running are ignored for that row.\n   The server action is idempotent, so a retry after a lost response is safe.\n5. **Strings** (`values`, `values-de/fr/es/it`): the error text and the\n   checkbox's content description.\n6. **Manual checks:** complete a todo (API 24 and 34+); complete a recurring\n   todo (the next occurrence appears after the re-fetch if it is due);\n   airplane mode (revert + error); complete a todo deleted in the app\n   meanwhile (row disappears); double tap; complete in the widget, then open\n   the app (the todo shows as completed).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Uncompleting from the widget (the server has no such action).\n- A retry queue for offline taps.\n- Actions on other rows or other widgets.\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017EbahFjScrvL6vxxaXrL5B","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
