{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MdXtGZBndGgGo3m1TPmaHp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"app widget collection setPendingIntentTemplate broadcast receiver start activity background activity launch restriction trampoline widget click\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"background activity starts\",\"url\":\"https://developer.android.com/preview/privacy/background-activity-starts\"},{\"title\":\"secure bal\",\"url\":\"https://developer.android.com/guide/components/activities/secure-bal?hl=fr\"},{\"title\":\"background starts\",\"url\":\"https://developer.android.com/guide/components/activities/background-starts?hl=uk\"},{\"title\":\"secure bal\",\"url\":\"https://developer.android.com/guide/components/activities/secure-bal\"},{\"title\":\"secure bal\",\"url\":\"https://developer.android.com/guide/components/activities/secure-bal?authuser=8\"},{\"title\":\"git.aicp-rom.com\",\"url\":\"https://git.aicp-rom.com/frameworks_base.git/plain/core/java/android/app/ComponentOptions.java\"},{\"title\":\"secure bal\",\"url\":\"https://developer.android.com/guide/components/activities/secure-bal?hl=zh-cn\"},{\"title\":\"developer.android.google.cn\",\"url\":\"https://developer.android.google.cn/reference/kotlin/android/widget/RemoteViews.RemoteResponse?authuser=5\"},{\"title\":\"secure bal\",\"url\":\"https://developer.android.com/guide/components/activities/secure-bal?hl=it\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up anything that addresses widget click handling and background activity launch (BAL) together. It returned two relevant threads, and I can't confirm how they apply to your specific widget setup.\n\n**Collection template mechanics:** The RemoteViews reference says that setting a PendingIntent on each collection item is expensive, so developers are steered toward one shared template on the collection. Each item then supplies a fill-in intent that gets merged into that template to form the final click intent. Setting PendingIntents on individual items is costly and not recommended. A single template can be set on the collection, with per-item click actions distinguished by a fillInIntent.\n\n**Background launch restrictions:** Android 10 and later limit when apps can start activities from the background. A BAL is defined to include a launch triggered through a PendingIntent received from a different app. A Background Activity Launch occurs when an app not in the foreground, with no visible activities, or a PendingIntent received from a different app attempts to start a new activity.\n\n**Opt-in rules:** For a launch to succeed, either the app that created the PendingIntent or the app that sends it must opt in. For apps targeting Android 15 or higher, the creator no longer grants this privilege implicitly. Apps targeting Android 15 or higher will default to no longer implicitly granting background activity launch privileges to PendingIntents they create. The sender can opt in through ActivityOptions, using the setPendingIntentBackgroundActivityStartMode method on the options passed to send().\n\n**Implication for widgets:** Widget clicks are typically handled by the launcher, and the template's PendingIntent is sent from the launcher's process. Whether a broadcast-receiver-then-startActivity \"trampoline\" still gets BAL privileges depends on the creator and sender opt-in settings, and this search didn't cover that case. The official Android BAL and PendingIntent docs are the best next place to check, especially the creator-side opt-in section.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1bd9fed-904f-4ef7-b990-1d5b7016b4d3","uuid":"5aa3d33f-f9ee-4221-aec4-e47a62ae9f79","timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:57:31.235Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"app widget collection setPendingIntentTemplate broadcast receiver start activity background activity launch restriction trampoline widget click"