{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgWtBTVNh1wbct4oGKvLF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote 9 tasks to `docs/jobs/motivation_tap-to-complete-on-the-your-day-widget/tasks.md`. The branch is the job's branch. All the work is native Android code: nothing changes in `frontend/` or `patch/`, and no new dependencies are needed.\n\n**What the tasks cover**\n- Read the `action` field on each widget row, and only keep it when its type and key are valid.\n- Send the action to the server and handle each status code from the brief's table.\n- Remember which rows have a call running and which failed, so the widget can show them as done or reverted.\n- Add a private receiver for checkbox taps and a background job per row, so a second tap on the same row does nothing.\n- Add the checkbox itself: a real checkbox on API 31+ and a tappable icon on 24–30.\n- Show the error state, add the strings in all five languages, then build and do the manual checks.\n\n**Three things the developer has to settle first** (all noted at the top of the file):\n1. **Highest risk, the shared tap handler.** The list allows only one tap handler for all its rows, and right now it opens the app. A checkbox tap would go through the same handler and open the app too. The obvious fix is to send every tap to the new receiver, which then opens the app for normal row taps. But Android may block that on API 34/35+, because the app targets SDK 36. This could break the existing \"tap a row to open it\" behaviour, so it has to be tested on API 24, 31 and 35+. The task tells the developer to stop and report back if it doesn't work.\n2. **Background work below API 31.** The brief asks for an expedited background job. On those older versions that needs a notification, which means one more string than the brief lists. The developer should flag it if it's needed.\n3. **Id format.** The brief says to validate the todo id but doesn't say what a valid one looks like. I assumed letters, digits and dashes, up to 64 characters, which covers UUIDs.\n\nI checked Android's docs on background activity launches for point 1 but found nothing specific to widget taps, which is why it stays a test-on-device item:\n- [Background activity starts](https://developer.android.com/guide/components/activities/background-starts?hl=uk)\n- [Secure background activity launches](https://developer.android.com/guide/components/activities/secure-bal)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3497,"cache_read_input_tokens":55264,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3497},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1bd9fed-904f-4ef7-b990-1d5b7016b4d3","uuid":"320fbce8-0179-4212-8265-fbc0d6732563","timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:58:25.150Z","request_id":"req_011CgWtBT45jvAciyWwc5JU4"}
