{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgWtaPCJFSHdMWkjZNoRv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written tap-to-complete for the Your Day widget and committed it on `feature/motivation_tap-to-complete-on-the-your-day-widget`, but it has never been compiled or run. This environment has no JDK or Android SDK, so `./gradlew assembleDebug` and all the manual checks from the brief are still to do.\n\n**What it does now:**\n- Todo rows that carry a `check` action show a checkbox: a real one on API 31+, a tappable icon on 24–30. Rows with an unknown action type, a bad key or a bad id get no control.\n- A tap goes to a new receiver (not exported) that checks the tap against the cached widget data, ticks the row straight away and queues one background job per row, so double taps are ignored.\n- That job sends `POST /api/v1/widgets/actions/{key}/{id}` with the widget token and follows the brief's status table:\n  - **200 / 403 / 404:** the row stays ticked and all widgets re-fetch.\n  - **401:** the token is deleted and the widget shows the signed-out state.\n  - **426:** the row is unticked and the widget shows \"Please update the app\".\n  - **429 / 5xx / offline:** the row is unticked and the header shows \"Couldn't complete\". Nothing is retried.\n- The two new strings are added in en, de, fr, es and it.\n\n**Things to check or decide:**\n- **Row taps that open the app may break on newer Android.** A list widget can only have one tap target, so ordinary row taps now also go through the new receiver, which then opens the app. On Android 14/15 and up, opening the app from a receiver like that may be blocked. I expect it to work but couldn't test it. Please try a row tap on API 24, 31 and 35+. If it's blocked, the design needs your decision.\n- **The job is only \"expedited\" on API 31+.** Below 31, expediting means showing a notification, so there I left it as a normal background job, which usually runs right away. Please confirm that reading of the brief.\n- **Row id format:** I assumed ids match `[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,64}`, which covers UUIDs. Rows with other ids get no checkbox.\n- **Kept rows ticked during a refresh:** a refresh that lands while the call is still running keeps the row ticked, which is a small deviation from the task text. Ticked rows also clear themselves after 5 minutes, so a row can't stay stuck as done.\n- **Manifest change:** the new receiver adds an entry to `AndroidManifest.xml`, so it needs review.\n- **Possible older bug, not touched:** a row's subtitle and time label may leak onto another row when the list reuses its views. Worth watching during the manual checks.\n\nThe full write-up, with the list of manual checks, is in `docs/jobs/motivation_tap-to-complete-on-the-your-day-widget/implementation.md`. Nothing is pushed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":480,"cache_read_input_tokens":89855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":480},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bed1ea8c-a279-4a02-b21e-f558df4812a3","uuid":"9a5bfbaf-3cbc-4bb2-b280-f6774275ab3f","timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:03:36.660Z","request_id":"req_011CgWtaNsTUKjphK7KLYJrN"}
