{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\nbrief.md\nimplementation.md\nsession.log\ntasks.md\ntokens.json\nverdict.md\n# Brief: tap-to-complete on the \"Your Day\" widget\n\ntype: feature\nid: motivation\nbranch: feature/motivation_tap-to-complete-on-the-your-day-widget\ndate: 2026-10-29\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nTodo rows on the Your Day widget get a checkbox. Tapping it completes the\ntodo on the server and updates the widget. This is built as generic action\nplumbing that every later interactive widget reuses.\n\nThis is job 6 of 6 in `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets-decisions.md`\n(D3, D8, D11). Read that document first. It depends on\n[[android-widget-foundation-your-day]] and on the API's\n`POST /widgets/actions/todo.complete/{todo}`.\n\n## Why\n\nCompleting a todo is the most common thing users do on Your Day. Building it\nnow also proves the interaction path (intents, background calls, error and\nrevert states) before other widgets depend on it.\n\n## Contract with the API\n\nThe API lives in another repo and is not visible from here. This section is\nthe complete contract this job relies on; the widget data format, headers and\ngeneral status codes are in [[android-widget-foundation-your-day]].\n\nRows that can be acted on carry, for example:\n`\"action\": { \"type\": \"check\", \"key\": \"todo.complete\", \"checked\": false }`.\n\nRequest: `POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/{key}/{id}`, for example\n`POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/todo.complete/<todo uuid>`, with the same\nheaders as the widget fetch (`Authorization: Bearer <widget token>`,\n`Accept: application/json`, `X-Client-Version`) and no body.\n\n| Status | Meaning | Native does |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 | Done (envelope with `data: null`). Also returned when the todo was already completed: the action is idempotent | Re-fetch all placed widgets |\n| 401 | Widget token invalid or expired | Delete the local token, show the signed-out state |\n| 403 | The todo belongs to someone else (should not happen from widget data) | Treat like 404 |\n| 404 | The todo no longer exists, or the server has no such action | Re-fetch |\n| 426 | App below the server's minimum version | Revert the row, show \"Please update the app\" |\n| 429 / 5xx / no response | Rate-limited, server or network problem | Revert the row, show a short error state |\n\nCompleting a recurring todo creates its next occurrence on the server; the\nre-fetch shows it if it is due. There is no \"uncomplete\" action.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Generic action handling:** rows with\n   `action: { type, key, checked? }`. Native knows UI **types** only; for now\n   `check`. Rows with an unknown type render without the control. The `key`\n   is posted as-is to `POST /widgets/actions/{key}/{id}` after validating its\n   format (`[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]*`) and the id; native has no per-key code.\n2. **Checkbox:** on API 31+ a real checkbox (`setCompoundButtonChecked` +\n   `RemoteViews.RemoteResponse`); on 24–30 a tappable checkbox icon. Same\n   behaviour on both.\n3. **Flow:** tap → explicit, non-exported receiver (fill-in extras are\n   untrusted: validate them) → the row shows as done at once → an expedited\n   WorkManager job calls the action with the widget token (read from the\n   token store, not from input data) → on success re-fetch all placed widgets.\n4. **Errors (D11):**\n   - 404: the todo is gone, re-fetch;\n   - 401: signed-out state, delete the local token;\n   - offline, 429, 5xx: revert the row and show a short error state on the\n     widget; nothing is queued for later;\n   - repeated taps while a call is running are ignored for that row.\n   The server action is idempotent, so a retry after a lost response is safe.\n5. **Strings** (`values`, `values-de/fr/es/it`): the error text and the\n   checkbox's content description.\n6. **Manual checks:** complete a todo (API 24 and 34+); complete a recurring\n   todo (the next occurrence appears after the re-fetch if it is due);\n   airplane mode (revert + error); complete a todo deleted in the app\n   meanwhile (row disappears); double tap; complete in the widget, then open\n   the app (the todo shows as completed).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Uncompleting from the widget (the server has no such action).\n- A retry queue for offline taps.\n- Actions on other rows or other widgets.\nIf something needs more privileges the human will test. Don't break the pipeline.\nfeature/motivation_tap-to-complete-on-the-your-day-widget\n# Tasks: tap-to-complete on the \"Your Day\" widget\n\nid: motivation\nanalyst: @analyst\ndate: 2026-10-29\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context\n\nThe read-only foundation (job 5) is already on this branch under\n`android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/widget/`: `YourDayWidgetProvider`\n(render), `YourDayPayload` (parse), `WidgetApi` (HTTP), `WidgetFetchWorker`\n+ `WidgetWork` (WorkManager, `work-runtime` 2.11.2), `WidgetCache`,\n`WidgetTokenStore`. All work here is Android-native. Nothing in `frontend/`\nor `patch/` changes, and no new dependencies are needed.\n\n## Open questions / risks to resolve first\n\n1. **One click template per coll\n\n... [9724 characters truncated] ...\n\nthat action, not already checked. It then calls\n`startAction`, re-renders and enqueues the job. Route taps are forwarded to\n`MainActivity` (`ACTION_WIDGET_ROUTE` + the existing extras,\n`FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK`), which keeps validating them as before.\n**Manifest change: please review.**\n\nTASK-5 (`WidgetActionWorker.java` (new), `WidgetWork.java`): `runAction()`\nenqueues unique work `widget-action-<id>` with `KEEP`. The input data is only\nthe key and id; the worker reads the token and URL from `WidgetTokenStore`. The\noutcomes are:\n- OK/404: the row stays done and `fetchNow` runs.\n- 401: `clearIfCurrent` + `WidgetCache.clear`.\n- 426: revert + `UPDATE_APP`.\n- Anything else: revert + the error flag.\n\nNo retry in any case. If the token changes mid-call, the row is reverted\nsilently. `cancelAll` also cancels action work, by tag.\n\nTASK-6 (`layout/widget_your_day_row.xml`, `layout-v31/widget_your_day_row.xml`\n(new), `drawable/ic_widget_check_on.xml` (new), `YourDayWidgetProvider.java`):\n- On API 31+, rows use a real `CheckBox` with `setCompoundButtonChecked` and\n  `setOnCheckedChangeResponse(RemoteResponse.fromFillInIntent(...))`. Checked\n  rows are disabled.\n- On 24–30, rows use a tappable `ImageView`. Unchecked reuses\n  `ic_widget_todo` (the circle); checked uses the new filled circle-check.\n- The control is checked when the server says `checked` or the row's action\n  is active, and every render sets the state explicitly, so reverts undo the\n  launcher's local toggle.\n- The fill-in is always set, and the unused icon or checkbox is hidden\n  explicitly, so a recycled list view never keeps another row's intent or\n  control. The receiver ignores taps on checked or active rows.\n- Action rows show the checkbox in place of the todo icon.\n\nTASK-7 (`YourDayWidgetProvider.java`): while the error flag is set, the\nheader's \"Updated …\" line shows `widget_action_failed`. The flag clears on\nthe next successful fetch or the next tap. No layout change was needed.\n\nTASK-8 (`values`, `values-de/fr/es/it` `strings.xml`): adds\n`widget_action_failed` and `widget_action_check` (the content description).\nNo notification strings were needed (see below).\n\nTASK-9: not done. There was no toolchain, so nothing was built, and the\nmanual checks are still open:\n\n| Check | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `./gradlew assembleDebug` | not done (no JDK/SDK here) |\n| Complete a todo, API 24 | not done |\n| Complete a todo, API 34+ | not done |\n| Complete a recurring todo (next occurrence appears if due) | not done |\n| Airplane mode → revert + error | not done |\n| Todo deleted in the app meanwhile → row disappears | not done |\n| Double tap → one call | not done |\n| Complete in widget, then open app → shown completed | not done |\n| **Row tap → opens route, API 24 / 31 / 35+ (regression)** | not done |\n\nRework after review: a rejected check tap (row not in the cache, state not\nOK, already checked or already running) now re-renders the widget, so the\nlauncher's local CheckBox toggle on API 31+ is undone.\n(`WidgetActionReceiver.java`)\n\nRework round, still blocked: this environment still has no JDK, Android SDK\nor emulator, so the build, the row-tap regression on API 24/31/35+ and the\nstep 6 checks remain open. They need a human with an Android toolchain.\n\n## Decisions / assumptions\n\n- **Open question 1 (trampoline): unverified.** Row taps now go\n  launcher → broadcast → receiver → `startActivity(MainActivity)`. I expect\n  this to work: the widget host sends the click while it is visible, and a\n  broadcast `PendingIntent` sent that way gives the receiving process a short\n  background-activity-start window. On API 34+ that depends on the host\n  allowing BAL when it sends the `PendingIntent`, which the framework's\n  default RemoteViews click handling does. I could not check this on a\n  device. If row taps fail to open the app on 35+, the design needs a human\n  decision, as the analyst noted.\n- **Open question 2 (expedited below 31):** the job is expedited only on\n  API 31+. Below 31 it is normal one-time work with no constraints, which\n  usually runs right away. This avoids a foreground-service notification,\n  its channel and its strings. It is a deliberate reading of the brief's\n  \"expedited\": please confirm.\n- **Open question 3 (id format):** row ids must match `[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,64}`,\n  which is path-segment safe and covers UUIDs. Rows with other ids (or a\n  numeric JSON id) get no checkbox.\n- 403 on an action is treated like 404, as the brief says: the row stays done\n  and a re-fetch follows.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- The build and all manual checks are still outstanding (see TASK-9).\n- Existing, not changed: `itemView` only *shows* the optional subtitle, time\n  and icon. Since the list reapplies item views to recycled views, a row\n  without a subtitle could in theory keep a recycled row's subtitle. Worth\n  checking during the manual tests. The new checkbox and icon handling hides\n  them explicitly.\ncat: /workspace/.manigot/manigot.json: No such file or directory","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_013a46ncdSfKu6A2yNkVC1vY"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84e3245c-e64c-44d1-9af3-cab57c31f3fd","uuid":"6afc2548-4270-4755-b36b-25ec697f5f0a","timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:22:05.548Z","tool_use_result":"Error: Exit code 1\nbrief.md\nimplementation.md\nsession.log\ntasks.md\ntokens.json\nverdict.md\n# Brief: tap-to-complete on the \"Your Day\" widget\n\ntype: feature\nid: motivation\nbranch: feature/motivation_tap-to-complete-on-the-your-day-widget\ndate: 2026-10-29\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nTodo rows on the Your Day widget get a checkbox. Tapping it completes the\ntodo on the server and updates the widget. This is built as generic action\nplumbing that every later interactive widget reuses.\n\nThis is job 6 of 6 in `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets-decisions.md`\n(D3, D8, D11). Read that document first. It depends on\n[[android-widget-foundation-your-day]] and on the API's\n`POST /widgets/actions/todo.complete/{todo}`.\n\n## Why\n\nCompleting a todo is the most common thing users do on Your Day. Building it\nnow also proves the interaction path (intents, background calls, error and\nrevert states) before other widgets depend on it.\n\n## Contract with the API\n\nThe API lives in another repo and is not visible from here. This section is\nthe complete contract this job relies on; the widget data format, headers and\ngeneral status codes are in [[android-widget-foundation-your-day]].\n\nRows that can be acted on carry, for example:\n`\"action\": { \"type\": \"check\", \"key\": \"todo.complete\", \"checked\": false }`.\n\nRequest: `POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/{key}/{id}`, for example\n`POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/todo.complete/<todo uuid>`, with the same\nheaders as the widget fetch (`Authorization: Bearer <widget token>`,\n`Accept: application/json`, `X-Client-Version`) and no body.\n\n| Status | Meaning | Native does |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 | Done (envelope with `data: null`). Also returned when the todo was already completed: the action is idempotent | Re-fetch all placed widgets |\n| 401 | Widget token invalid or expired | Delete the local token, show the signed-out state |\n| 403 | The todo belongs to someone else (should not happen from widget data) | Treat like 404 |\n| 404 | The todo no longer exists, or the server has no such action | Re-fetch |\n| 426 | App below the server's minimum version | Revert the row, show \"Please update the app\" |\n| 429 / 5xx / no response | Rate-limited, server or network problem | Revert the row, show a short error state |\n\nCompleting a recurring todo creates its next occurrence on the server; the\nre-fetch shows it if it is due. There is no \"uncomplete\" action.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Generic action handling:** rows with\n   `action: { type, key, checked? }`. Native knows UI **types** only; for now\n   `check`. Rows with an unknown type render without the control. The `key`\n   is posted as-is to `POST /widgets/actions/{key}/{id}` after validating its\n   format (`[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]*`) and the id; native has no per-key code.\n2. **Checkbox:** on API 31+ a real checkbox (`setCompoundButtonChecked` +\n   `RemoteViews.RemoteResponse`); on 24–30 a tappable checkbox icon. Same\n   behaviour on both.\n3. **Flow:** tap → explicit, non-exported receiver (fill-in extras are\n   untrusted: validate them) → the row shows as done at once → an expedited\n   WorkManager job calls the action with the widget token (read from the\n   token store, not from input data) → on success re-fetch all placed widgets.\n4. **Errors (D11):**\n   - 404: the todo is gone, re-fetch;\n   - 401: signed-out state, delete the local token;\n   - offline, 429, 5xx: revert the row and show a short error state on the\n     widget; nothing is queued for later;\n   - repeated taps while a call is running are ignored for that row.\n   The server action is idempotent, so a retry after a lost response is safe.\n5. **Strings** (`values`, `values-de/fr/es/it`): the error text and the\n   checkbox's content description.\n6. **Manual checks:** complete a todo (API 24 and 34+); complete a recurring\n   todo (the next occurrence appears after the re-fetch if it is due);\n   airplane mode (revert + error); complete a todo deleted in the app\n   meanwhile (row disappears); double tap; complete in the widget, then open\n   the app (the todo shows as completed).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Uncompleting from the widget (the server has no such action).\n- A retry queue for offline taps.\n- Actions on other rows or other widgets.\nIf something needs more privileges the human will test. Don't break the pipeline.\nfeature/motivation_tap-to-complete-on-the-your-day-widget\n# Tasks: tap-to-complete on the \"Your Day\" widget\n\nid: motivation\nanalyst: @analyst\ndate: 2026-10-29\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context\n\nThe read-only foundation (job 5) is already on this branch under\n`android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/widget/`: `YourDayWidgetProvider`\n(render), `YourDayPayload` (parse), `WidgetApi` (HTTP), `WidgetFetchWorker`\n+ `WidgetWork` (WorkManager, `work-runtime` 2.11.2), `WidgetCache`,\n`WidgetTokenStore`. All work here is Android-native. Nothing in `frontend/`\nor `patch/` changes, and no new dependencies are needed.\n\n## Open questions / risks to resolve first\n\n1. **One click template per coll\n\n... [9724 characters truncated] ...\n\nthat action, not already checked. It then calls\n`startAction`, re-renders and enqueues the job. Route taps are forwarded to\n`MainActivity` (`ACTION_WIDGET_ROUTE` + the existing extras,\n`FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_T