{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 2\n# Tasks: tap-to-complete on the \"Your Day\" widget\n\nid: motivation\nanalyst: @analyst\ndate: 2026-10-29\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context\n\nThe read-only foundation (job 5) is already on this branch under\n`android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/widget/`: `YourDayWidgetProvider`\n(render), `YourDayPayload` (parse), `WidgetApi` (HTTP), `WidgetFetchWorker`\n+ `WidgetWork` (WorkManager, `work-runtime` 2.11.2), `WidgetCache`,\n`WidgetTokenStore`. All work here is Android-native. Nothing in `frontend/`\nor `patch/` changes, and no new dependencies are needed.\n\n## Open questions / risks to resolve first\n\n1. **One click template per collection (affects TASK-4).** The list has a\n   single `setPendingIntentTemplate`. Today it is an **activity**\n   `PendingIntent` to `MainActivity` (row tap → route). Every fill-in in a\n   row, the checkbox included, merges into that same template. That holds for\n   `RemoteResponse.fromFillInIntent` on API 31+ as well. So a checkbox tap\n   cannot reach a broadcast receiver unless the template changes. The obvious\n   fix is a **broadcast** template to a new non-exported receiver that\n   handles checks itself and forwards route taps to `MainActivity`. But\n   starting an activity from a receiver is a background activity launch, and\n   this app targets SDK 36, where a `PendingIntent` creator no longer grants\n   BAL implicitly. Row taps that open the app could then break on API 34/35+.\n   The developer must verify this on API 24, 31 and 35+ before building on it.\n   If the trampoline is blocked, stop and report back rather than invent a\n   different design.\n2. **Expedited work below API 31.** On API < 31, WorkManager runs expedited\n   work as a foreground service. The worker must then provide\n   `getForegroundInfo()`, which needs a notification, a channel and a string.\n   Otherwise it fails at runtime. The brief asks for \"expedited\". If that would\n   mean adding a notification and its strings, flag it in implementation.md as\n   an addition beyond the brief's string list.\n3. **Id format.** The brief says to \"validate the id\" but gives no format, and\n   the contract example is a todo UUID. The assumption is\n   `[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,64}`, path-segment safe and covering UUIDs. Write it down in\n   implementation.md.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Parse the optional row `action: { type, key, checked? }` and the row `id` in `YourDayPayload`. Keep the action only when `type` is a known UI type (`check`), `key` matches `[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]*` (length-capped like `MainActivity.ROUTE_KEY`) and the row id is valid; otherwise the row has no action.\n  files: android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/widget/YourDayPayload.java\n  depends: none\n  risk: low. The parse is additive, and unknown types already fall through to \"no control\".\n\nTASK-2: Add `WidgetApi.postAction(context, apiUrl, token, key, id)`. It sends `POST /api/v1/widgets/actions/{key}/{id}` with the same headers, redirects off and no body. It re-validates key/id and maps 200→OK, 401→UNAUTHORIZED, 403/404→NOT_FOUND, 426→UPGRADE_REQUIRED, and everything else or an exception→TEMPORARY_FAILURE. Share the connection setup with `fetchYourDay` instead of duplicating it.\n  files: android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/widget/WidgetApi.java\n  depends: none\n  risk: low. The pattern already exists. Path segments must come only from validated values and never be logged.\n\nTASK-3: Add per-row interaction state to `WidgetCache`: the set of row ids with a call in flight (shown as done), a row-error state (reverted row + a short error flag, cleared by the next successful fetch or tap), and clear both in `clear()`/`saveData()`.\n  files: android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/widget/WidgetCache.java\n  depends: none\n  risk: medium. Stale \"pending\" entries (process death mid-call) must not stick forever. Tie them to the next fetch or to a timestamp.\n\nTASK-4: Add an explicit, non-exported `WidgetActionReceiver` (manifest entry) and switch the list's click template to it. Validate the fill-in extras (type/key/id format, plus `id` present in the current cached payload with that action). Ignore the tap if the row is already pending. Otherwise mark it pending, re-render, and enqueue the action work. Forward route taps to `MainActivity` with the existing extras. See open question 1.\n  files: android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/widget/WidgetActionReceiver.java (new), android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/widget/YourDayWidgetProvider.java, android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml\n  depends: TASK-1, TASK-3, TASK-5\n  risk: high. Changing the template can break the existing row-tap → open-route path (BAL restrictions at targetSdk 36). It is also a manifest change, which needs a reviewer flag.\n\nTASK-5: Add `WidgetActionWorker` plus a `WidgetWork.runAction(context, key, id)`. Run it as unique work per row id (`KEEP`, so repeated taps are no-ops) and expedited with `RUN_AS_NON_EXPEDITED_WORK_REQUEST`, with only key and id as input data. The worker reads the token and URL fro\n\n... [3616 characters truncated] ...\n\nall\nhas the right arity (11 args).\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `WidgetApi.postAction` re-validates key and id, sends an empty POST\n(`setFixedLengthStreamingMode(0)`) with the shared headers and redirects off,\nand maps 200/401/403/404/426/other/exception as specified. The extracted\n`open()` keeps `fetchYourDay` unchanged: 403 still ends up as\nTEMPORARY_FAILURE there, as before.\n\nTASK-3: PASS\nnotes: `WidgetCache.java`: running and finished entries are tracked with a\n5-minute TTL, so stale entries cannot stick. `saveData` keeps entries that\nare still running (a deliberate, documented deviation, and correct).\n`clear()` wipes the action state. Mutators are `synchronized`.\n\nTASK-4: PARTIAL\nnotes: The code is correct. The receiver is explicit and\n`exported=\"false\"`. It validates type, key and id, and requires the row to be\nin the cached payload with that action and not already checked. Route taps are\nforwarded to `MainActivity`, which still validates them. However, open\nquestion 1 (does the broadcast → `startActivity` trampoline still open the\napp for row taps on API 34/35+ at targetSdk 36?) is **unverified**. The\nanalyst made device verification on API 24, 31 and 35+ a precondition, and if\nit is blocked, row taps (an existing, shipped feature) stop working. Minor:\non API 31+ the launcher toggles the CheckBox locally, so a tap the receiver\nrejects (row missing from the cache, or state not OK) leaves the box checked\nuntil the next render, because the early returns do not call `updateAll`.\n\nTASK-5: PASS\nnotes: Unique work per row with `KEEP`. Input data holds only the key and id,\nand the token comes from `WidgetTokenStore`. The status table is applied as\nthe brief specifies, a token swap mid-call is handled, nothing is retried, and\n`cancelAll` cancels by tag. Expedited only on API 31+ (open question 2): this\nis sound, because a plain `Worker` enqueued as expedited below 31 has no\n`getForegroundInfo` and would fail at runtime. The deviation is documented.\n\nTASK-6: PASS\nnotes: `layout-v31` uses a real `CheckBox` with `setCompoundButtonChecked`\nand `RemoteResponse.fromFillInIntent`. Below 31 a tappable `ImageView`\nswitches between `ic_widget_todo` and `ic_widget_check_on`. The state, the\nfill-in and the visibility are set on every render, so recycled views and\nreverts are handled. The content description is set.\n\nTASK-7: PASS\nnotes: The header's \"Updated\" line shows `widget_action_failed` while the\nflag is set. The flag is cleared by `saveData` and `startAction`.\n\nTASK-8: PASS\nnotes: Both strings exist in `values`, `-de`, `-fr`, `-es` and `-it`, and the\ntranslations are fine.\n\nTASK-9: FAIL\nnotes: Nothing was compiled (`./gradlew assembleDebug` was not run, because\nthere is no JDK or SDK in the agent environment), and none of the brief's\nstep 6 manual checks were done. That includes the row-tap regression on\nAPI 24, 31 and 35+. I could not build it either.\n\n## Security\n\nNot run separately. From this review: the receiver is non-exported and\nexplicit. Fill-in extras are validated and cross-checked against the cache.\nURL path segments come only from validated values. The token never goes into\nWorkManager input data, and redirects are disabled. No concerns.\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nThe code reads correctly, but it has never been compiled or run, and the\nhigh-risk design assumption is unverified. These need a human with an Android\ntoolchain and devices or emulators:\n\n1. Build it: `cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug` must succeed.\n2. Verify the row-tap → open-route path (now a broadcast trampoline) on\n   API 24, 31 and 35+. If it is blocked on 34/35+, the design needs a human\n   decision, as the analyst said (tasks.md, open question 1).\n3. Run the brief's step 6 checks and record the results in\n   implementation.md: complete a todo on API 24 and 34+, complete a\n   recurring todo, airplane mode (revert + error), a todo deleted in the app\n   meanwhile, double tap, and complete in the widget then open the app.\n=====\n3f615a1 [motivation] chore: commit all\n5627f54 [motivation] chore: commit all\nd6171bd [motivation] chore: commit all\n67eb2a7 [motivation] implementation: note rework round\na23d32a Re-render widget after a rejected checkbox tap\n32e6d95 [motivation] chore: commit all\nda05392 [motivation] verdict: needs work, unbuilt and unverified\n45a34aa [motivation] chore: commit all\n0eb49a4 [motivation] implementation: add summary\nf400a54 Add widget action strings\n3c65ecc Show the widget action error state in the header\n164faf4 Show a checkbox on Your Day rows with a check action\n1cbd8ec Route widget row taps through WidgetActionReceiver\na52db47 Add WidgetActionWorker and WidgetWork.runAction\nd81ad91 Expire finished widget actions too\nb4