{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgWv2JhmPFh7XGbFxNFeU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've approved the job, but the code has never been compiled or run on a device. Nobody has built it or tried it on a phone yet. The verdict is committed in `verdict.md` (80b87e0).\n\n**What changed since the last review:** one fix. On Android 12+, the launcher ticks the checkbox itself before the app decides anything. When the app now rejects a tap (for example, the todo is no longer on the widget), it redraws the widget so the checkbox unticks again. That was the small issue from the last round, and it's correct now.\n\n**Why it's approved this time:** the last review said \"needs work\" only because nothing had been built or tested on a device. The brief now says checks that need more privileges will be done by a human. So the approval comes from that new line in the brief, not from new evidence that the code works.\n\n**Before release, someone needs to:**\n1. Build it with `cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug`.\n2. Check that tapping a todo row still opens that todo in the app on Android 7, 12 and 15+. This is the biggest risk. Row taps now go through a new receiver before opening the app, and Android 14+ may block that. If they do, the design needs a decision before shipping.\n3. Run the brief's step 6 checks: complete a todo, complete a recurring one, airplane mode, a todo deleted in the app meanwhile, double tap, and complete on the widget then open the app. They're all listed as \"not done\" in `implementation.md`.\n\nThe change also adds a new receiver to `AndroidManifest.xml`, so that file needs a human look as well."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1441,"cache_read_input_tokens":29541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1441},"output_tokens":5,"service_t